# wip — interpretation-trials
# Started: 2026-11-06

#>plan_interpretation_trials
#:plan #!public_interest_research
#:layer #!semantics

?["card"]{
 phase: #seed
 gist: "Open readings of Spw's marks held as trials, each scored expressive, interactive and grounded before it becomes grammar"
 touches: [~".agents/plans/interpretation-trials"]
 entry: ~"./interpretation-trials.spw"
 next: "The owner picks a card when ready; ~[trial_bench] can come first so each trial starts from every reader's reading side by side."
}

^["edges"]{
 feeds: [~"../brace-slot-reading/wip.spw", ~"../syntax-hardware-alignment/wip.spw", ~"../inquiry-loop/wip.spw", ~"../ground-edge-reading/wip.spw", ~"../relationship-contours/wip.spw", ~"../onboarding-quest/wip.spw"]
 shares: [~"../reading-drift/wip.spw", ~"../editor-inspection-instruments/wip.spw", ~"../plan-ecology-clustering/wip.spw"]
}

^["roots"]{
 @plan: ~".agents/plans/interpretation-trials/PLAN.md"
 @trials: ~".agents/plans/interpretation-trials/interpretation-trials.spw"
 @brainstorm: ~".spw/caches/journal/2026-11-06-reading-brainstorm.spw"
 @progressive: ~"packages/spw-seed/src/ir/progressive.ts"
}

^["intent"]{
 ~#goal: "Spw grows toward novel interactive semantics, and each step rests on something linguistically expressive (the owner, 2026-11-06)"
 ~#taste: "Try readings on purpose before deciding them; keep a reading when it lets a writer say more, lets a host do more, and mirrors how people already mean"
}

^["open"]{
 # Unresolved questions. When resolved: log in stream, then move to ^["done"] as ~#resolved(label).
 ?[first_trial]: "Which card runs first? The spaced = and the <…> readings move the most lines; the stages and guided-wonder cards move the most hosts."
 ?[bench_readers]: "Does the bench import the consumer's slot reader and factshift.center's line anatomy by path, read-only, or do those readers print their readings for the bench to collect?"
 ?[novice_trials]: "Are trial cards also quest material: can a newcomer run one, judge it, and leave an ask?"
}

^["commits"]{
 # Named, in order. Planned ~[name]; landed .[name](hash). Names are never reused.
 ~[trial_bench]: "^seed[analyzers] — read every form on a trial card through each reader (seed's parse and source products, and the consumer readers by path) and print the readings side by side, with the card's holes left open"
 ~[first_trials]: ".[plans] — the owner runs the first trials and fills judgment and answer; each card keeps its ~#expect, written before the run"
 ~[promote_kept_readings]: ".[plans] — a reading kept on all three axes moves to its home plan as a decision citing its trial; a reading dropped stays on the card with why"
}

^["stream"]{
 >>[2026-11-06 18:10] decide — The owner asked to record the day's lines of wonder and to test Spw's interpretations and utilities more intentionally later, and set a direction: novel interactive semantics, grounded in something linguistically expressive. Opened this plan to hold sixteen trial cards with the owner's feature-card method and a rubric: expressive, interactive, grounded, cost.
 >>[2026-11-06 18:10] observe — The readers already disagree on the same lines. Seed reads <person>home as two expressions where factshift.center reads a concept written first, and reads ecestudent@ece.120~?[transistors work.how] as four expressions where factshift.center reads two lines tied by @ and ~ bonds. factshift.center reads lines with its own slot reader (line-anatomy.ts) and carries an older workbench copy (fffab72, 2026-03-12) under its app.
 >>[2026-11-06 18:10] note — Two cards came from the owner mid-pass: guided wonder (a newcomer's imprecise wonder guided by constructs in existing scripts; grounded in recasts and construction grammar) and stages (one script on several canvases along a projection gradient; the workbench's source products tokens, structure and trace are the first rungs, and factshift.center's panels already read in three levels).
 >>[2026-11-06 18:10] note — Added wonder_trial_hash_format: how a slot hash is written (positional, a #-led name, or line-shaped). slotHash ships in seed as a primitive with no written form, at the owner's choice (2026-11-06), so a canvas host can try it for first layout and hue before the form is decided.
 >>[2026-11-06 20:20] note — Added wonder_trial_prime_actualize: both hosts now act in two steps (spw.quest primes an operator before it actualizes; factshift.center's tools prime and actualize), which may be Spw's own ~ potential and ! action, so a host's act history could be written as Spw.
 >>[2026-11-06 20:28] note — The owner decided that every pair may lead the word (2026-11-06), so wonder_trial_slot_order no longer asks whether order is allowed, only what it says: noise, voice, or information structure. A slot query is to be read as a line (the owner's leaning), which makes wonder_trial_typed_hole a question about what a hole reads as inside a line.
}

^["cache"]{
 ~#status: "seed"
 ~#base_ref: "main@dbd138dd"
 ~#rebased_at: ""
 ~#files_hot: ".agents/plans/interpretation-trials/interpretation-trials.spw"
 ~#next_commit: "trial_bench"
 ~#open_count: "3"
 ~#last_stream: "2026-11-06 20:28"
}

^["done"]{
}
